					<h1 class="title" title="Haldwani Tour">Haldwani Tour</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
<h3>Location and history </h3>
<p><b>Haldwani</b> along with its twin city <b>Kathgodam</b> is located in the <b>Nainital district</b> of <b>Uttarakhand</b> in <b>India</b>. 
Also known as the <b>‘gateway of Kumaon’, Haldwani</b> is the third largest city in terms of population. 
Established in the 19th century, it was renamed as Haldwani. </p>
<h3>Places of interest</h3>
<p>Haldwani has a lot to offer to the tourists. One of the <b>most attractive tourist spot</b> is the <b>Gaula Barrage</b>. 
A perfect spot for trekking, camping and sightseeing, Haldwani has become a <b>picnic spot</b> now owing to its 
scenic beauty and charm. It is situated on the banks of <b>river Gaula</b>, so in the earlier days this barrage 
was built for the purpose of irrigation. A lot of tourists visit this place on their way to Kumaon. 
The peace and tranquility of the <b>Hedakhan Ashram</b> also draws many tourists to visit this place. There are 
many beautiful temples and caves across the <b>Gaula river</b> and one can spend a whole day here without getting 
bored. It is also situated on the banks of river Gaula. This place is a must visit for all the tourists. </p>

<p>The <b>Chitrashila Ghat</b>, a vulnerable cremation ground of the Hindus is situated at <b>Ranighat</b>, 
about 8 km. from Haldwani. The Uttaryani fair is the main attraction here every year on the festival of <b>Makar 
Sankranti</b>. Located at Pantnagar, a part of <b>Tanda forest</b> is the Sanjay Van. About 23 km. from Haldwani, 
the Sanjay Van is a beautiful picnic spot of <b>picturesque sights</b>. <b>Bird watching</b> can also be done here. 
Rare migratory birds can be spotted here.</p>

<p>Some 22 kms from Haldwani is the <b>popular site of excursion</b> the <b>Sat Tal</b>. It is a fusion of 
seven freshwater lakes together. Often considered equivalent to the <b>Westmoreland of England</b> by the English, 
this place is indeed worth the comparison. All around the lakes are the beautiful dense oak and pine trees. There 
are other beautiful lakes and spots of <b>excursion nearby Haldwani</b>. They are the <b>Naukuchia Tal, Mukteshwar</b> 
and <b>the Bhim Tal</b>, all lovely places for excursion. The <b>Jim Corbett National Park</b> is about 55 km. from 
Haldwani. Being thee <b>oldest national park of India</b>, this park boasts of having about 448 species of wildlife and 
plants. </p>

<p>Other important places that can be visited are the various big industries, the shopping malls and the stadium of 
Haldwani. One can also make a visit to the grain, fruit and the vegetable market of this place because it is said 
to be the largest of its kind in the whole country. </p>




